## Why This Is Asked
This assesses practical use of a caching layer in a basic AWS setup, focusing on pattern choice, sizing, TTL, invalidation, and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Cache-aside pattern
- ElastiCache Redis basics (node type, shard, TTL, eviction)
- Integration with EC2 apps and ALB health checks
- Observability with CloudWatch

## Code Example
```java
// Pseudo code for cache-aside
value = cache.get(key);
if (value == null) {
  value = db.query(key);
  cache.set(key, value, ttlSeconds);
}
return value;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle hot keys or write bursts?
- What changes if you switch to DynamoDB with DAX vs Redis?
